  },
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The number of air molecules per <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;increased from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>19</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>19</mn></msup><mo>.</mo></math> The ratio of collision frequency of air molecules before and after the increase in number respectively is :</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>75</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>50</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The given data is&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>19</mn></msup><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>19</mn></msup></math></p><p>The mean time between two collision has the meaning of a period <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#964;</mi></math>, since it indicates the repetitive time intervals in which on average collisions take place. The reciprocal of the time <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#964;</mi></math> can be understood as the&nbsp;collision frequency<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>f</mi></math>, which indicates the number of collisions per unit time.The collision frequency&nbsp;is also directly proportional to the number molecules per unit volume.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>&#8733;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>&#964;</mi></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>&#8733;</mo><mi>n</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>1&#160;</mtext></msub><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>2&#160;</mtext></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>19</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>19</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
